WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.690
Every machine can hold

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:03.930
several AI subscriptions,

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:05.470
Claude and Codex on one,

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:07.150
Claude and Codex on another.

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:08.720
SpecWithCode connects

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:10.360
your machines over Tailscale

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.020
and watches every limit

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:13.000
and reset.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.150
You talk to one coordinator.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:16.650
It starts threads,

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:17.990
each with its own pull

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:18.670
request.

00:00:19.390 --> 00:00:20.440
Auto-resolve closes a

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:21.660
thread only when it's

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:22.440
merged,

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:23.880
green and approved.

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:25.530
Linux for speed,

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:28.090
the Mac to orchestrate.

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:28.610
SpecWithCode,

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:31.730
open source at specwithcode.dev.
